VeridianOS: KWin: no moc runs for headers without Q_OBJECT

AutoMoc printed "No relevant classes found. No output generated." for six
headers whose moc_<header>.cpp a source includes although the header
declares nothing for moc (no Q_OBJECT, Q_GADGET or Q_NAMESPACE):

- core/gbmgraphicsbufferallocator.cpp, core/shmgraphicsbufferallocator.cpp,
  wayland/textinput.cpp, plugins/screenshot/screenshot.cpp: the
  moc_<header>.cpp include is removed (the .cpp files' own ".moc" includes,
  for their Q_OBJECT classes, stay), as upstream master has done for the
  first three.
- wayland/idleinhibit_v1.cpp: includes moc_idleinhibit_v1_p.cpp for the
  private header, which has no QObject; the include is removed
  (moc_idleinhibit_v1.cpp, for the public header, stays; master likewise).
- rules.cpp is also compiled into the window rules KCM with KCMRULES
  defined, where rules.h's QObject is excluded and moc has nothing to
  generate. The KCM's directory marks that copy SKIP_AUTOMOC, and the
  moc_rules.cpp include is kept for KWin core only (#ifndef KCMRULES).

No generated code changes: moc produced nothing for these headers.

